Here are a few ways to write a JavaScript function to convert Celsius to Fahrenheit, ranging from a basic function to one with input validation.

### 1. Basic Function (Most Common)

This is the simplest and most direct way to write the conversion.

```javascript
/**
 * Converts a temperature from Celsius to Fahrenheit.
 * Formula: (Celsius * 9/5) + 32
 *
 * @param {number} celsius The temperature in Celsius.
 * @returns {number} The equivalent temperature in Fahrenheit.
 */
function celsiusToFahrenheit(celsius) {
  // The conversion formula
  const fahrenheit = (celsius * 9/5) + 32;
  return fahrenheit;
}

// --- Examples ---
